# Celly soft-guard preflight false positives

## Observation

The local router logged repeated `compacted anthropic payload` entries while
Celly was issuing ordinary tool-loop requests. The estimator reported roughly
958k tokens and the log showed 472 mapped-down messages, but the matching
Claude Code responses reported about 449k provider tokens against an 872k
context window. The JSON-length estimator therefore caused an unnecessary
request-local rewrite.

## Change

CielAiRouter now declares `preflight_prompt_compaction: false`. Ordinary
Anthropic-wire turns and native compact requests pass through unchanged; the
existing native client compaction and reactive provider-overflow recovery
remain responsible for actual pressure. Translated Codex checkpoints still
use the guarded path because their client cannot perform Anthropic-native
compaction itself.

## Verification

- Focused provider, compaction, Codex translated-checkpoint, request-policy,
  and vLLM tests: 69 passed, 15 subtests passed.
- Architecture contracts: 5 passed, 7 subtests passed.
- `python -m ruff check`: passed.
- A live-config probe with an oversized body reported an estimated 750,026
  tokens, called the soft compactor zero times, and returned the body unchanged.

## Truncated semantic checkpoint follow-up

- A later Celly run at 21:46-21:50 local time logged 120-second upstream
  requests and repeated `context_compact_failed ... completed_chunks=0/13`.
  The error detail was `truncated_summary`, not a 60-second timeout.
- The map phase previously retried only explicit provider context rejections.
  A finite summary that ended at its output limit aborted the entire checkpoint
  before one source chunk completed, so the same turn failed again.
- A truncated or incomplete summary response now splits its source chunk and
  regenerates the smaller segment, matching the existing bounded retry used for
  an explicit context rejection. Client cancellation, deadline exhaustion, and
  ambiguous provider failures still abort without replay.
- Added a regression test that forces the first map summary to truncate and
  verifies the split segments complete. The full context-compaction suite
  passed: 31 tests.

## Published and installed

- Fix commit `e83bea7`; no-ff merge `625faed32c8680615ea1f46b9f29bc0764c3b886`.
- CI run `39714827921` passed. Publish run `39714827923` passed and published
  `@one-ciel-ai/ciel-runtime@0.2.51-nightly.20261022-030938.625faed`.
- Global install now reports that exact version. The installed package contains
  both `preflight_prompt_compaction=False` and the truncated-summary retry path;
  an import-level installed-package check passed.
- Already-running Ciel Runtime processes keep their previously loaded Python
  modules in memory. A relaunched Celly/Ara session is required to activate the
  new package in those processes; no live conversation process was terminated.
